---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Sign Language Translator"
  description="About SignLanguage-Translator.com — a free American Sign Language and British Sign Language learning aid built by Firoz Khan of FK Digital Media."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">About</h1>

    <div class="prose-lg mt-6 space-y-5 text-slate-700">
      <p>
        <strong>SignLanguage-Translator.com</strong> is a free learning aid for
        American Sign Language (ASL) and British Sign Language (BSL). Type
        English text and see it broken into signs — word-level signs from our
        dictionaries where available, and fingerspelling for everything else.
      </p>
      <p>
        ASL and BSL are completely separate languages — different signs,
        different grammar, different fingerspelling alphabets (one-handed vs
        two-handed). Each dictionary on this site was researched independently,
        and the translator never substitutes a sign from one language into the
        other.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is built and maintained by <strong>Firoz Khan</strong> of{" "}
        <strong>FK Digital Media</strong>, with one goal: make the first steps
        of learning sign language accessible to anyone with a browser.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">What this site is</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>A vocabulary learning aid for ASL and BSL beginners</li>
        <li>A text-to-sign sequence translator with playback controls and an ASL/BSL toggle</li>
        <li>Growing dictionaries of common ASL (57) and BSL (47) words and phrases</li>
        <li>Fingerspelling references: one-handed ASL A–Z + 0–9, two-handed BSL A–Z + 1–5</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">What this site is not</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>
          <strong>Not a substitute for a qualified interpreter.</strong> For
          medical, legal, emergency, or other important communication, always
          use a certified interpreter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Not a grammar teacher.</strong> ASL and BSL each have their own
          grammar and word order, which differ from English. This tool shows
          vocabulary sign by sign; it does not rearrange sentences into either
          language's grammar.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Not a certification.</strong> Text descriptions are a starting
          point. Real fluency comes from learning with Deaf instructors and the
          Deaf community.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="rounded-xl border-l-4 border-amber-500 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3">
        We describe things honestly here: what the site can do, what it cannot
        do, and where human instruction is irreplaceable.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Who built this</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
        <img
          src="/images/firoz-khan.webp"
          alt="Firoz Khan"
          class="h-36 w-36 shrink-0 rounded-2xl object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Firoz Khan</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600">FK Digital Media</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
            An independent maker building free, honest web tools. Find me on:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <li>
              <a
                href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/firoz-khan-1153358a/"
                class="inline-block rounded-lg border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-indigo-700 hover:border-indigo-700"
              >
                LinkedIn
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                href="https://github.com/fkdigitalmedia"
                class="inline-block rounded-lg border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-indigo-700 hover:border-indigo-700"
              >
                GitHub
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                href="https://www.instagram.com/rtibyfiroz/"
                class="inline-block rounded-lg border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-indigo-700 hover:border-indigo-700"
              >
                Instagram
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">How sign descriptions are written</h2>
      <p>
        Every dictionary entry is a text-based, step-by-step guide researched from
        established references and rewritten in our own original words. ASL
        entries draw on Lifeprint, university teaching materials, and
        public-health resources; BSL entries on BSL SignBank, BDA-adjacent
        teaching materials, and BSL dictionaries. We deliberately do not use
        AI-generated hand images: a wrong or distorted handshape could teach a
        sign incorrectly. The BSL alphabet illustrations on this site are by
        Coloringbuddymike via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0). Commissioned
        photos and videos from qualified signers are the planned next upgrade
        for these dictionaries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
